# =============================================================================
# Marine Intelligence Weekly -- deployment exclusion list (.vercelignore)
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# The repository root is the static web root and `package.json` performs no
# build, so every file Vercel receives becomes a URL. Before this file, every
# tracked file shipped: authoring specs, verification records, governance docs
# and the toolchain were all served. The repository is public, so this is not
# a confidentiality control -- it is data minimisation: fewer accidental web
# surfaces, fewer deployed bytes, and no future tracked internal file becoming
# a site URL by default.
#
# HOW VERCEL READS IT (verified against the bundled CLI, `getVercelIgnore`)
#   * The CLI reads ONLY this file (or `.nowignore`) plus a fixed default list
#     (.git, .vercel, node_modules, .env.local, .env.*.local, __pycache__ ...).
#     It NEVER reads .gitignore. So without this file, a workstation
#     `vercel deploy` uploads every git-ignored local file too. Section A below
#     therefore mirrors .gitignore explicitly -- keep the two in step.
#   * The Git integration only ever sees tracked files, then applies this file.
#   * Semantics are gitignore-style (the `ignore` package): a trailing `/`
#     matches a directory, a leading `/` anchors to the repository root.
#
# CHECKED BY tools/security/deploy_surface.test.mjs, which evaluates these
# patterns with the same library semantics against (1) representative
# authoring-only paths that must be excluded, (2) synthetic sentinels in every
# git-ignored class that must stay excluded, and (3) every candidate runtime
# path that must remain deployable. Change this file and that test together.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A. MIRROR OF .gitignore -- local material that must never leave the machine
#    on a CLI deployment. Derived from .gitignore on 2026-08-15; every entry
#    there is repeated here.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env*
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.production.local
node_modules/
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log
package-lock.json
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
dist/
build/
.next/
out/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.git/
.vercel/

# Third-party source scans of examination papers -- never redistributed.
meoclass1/pastpapers/docs/*.pdf
# Local-only provenance record naming the third-party host of each source copy.
meoclass1/pastpapers/verification/LOCAL_SOURCE_PROVENANCE.md
# Coaching handouts -- never a verification source, never redistributed.
Notes-for-written-answers/
# Scratch output from the notes tooling.
tools/notes/_*.txt
# Founder's master question-bank spreadsheets -- unreleased bank.
docs/MIW-master-Question-bank/*.xlsx
# A named candidate's private study material.
meoclass1/pastpapers/docs/notes from candidate/
# True Source corpora -- verbatim IMO instrument text, private authoring layer.
Knowledge Central/
# Six-year QP intelligence, derived; carries unsolved-sitting wording and the
# third-party host's recurrence annotations.
meoclass1/pastpapers/intelligence/derived/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# B. WRITTEN-PRODUCT AUTHORING LAYER -- rich canonical inputs and internal
#    records. Proven not to be fetched by any candidate page: the runtime
#    reads /solvedQP/solvedqp_content_index.json only.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
meoclass1/pastpapers/specs/
meoclass1/pastpapers/verification/
meoclass1/pastpapers/docs/
meoclass1/pastpapers/intelligence/
meoclass1/pastpapers/sample/
meoclass1/pastpapers/known_traps.md
meoclass1/pastpapers/pastpapers_content_index.json
# Oral-product authoring records living beside the product pages.
meoclass1/known_traps.md
meoclass1/qb_health_check.py

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# C. TOOLCHAIN AND REPOSITORY GOVERNANCE -- scripts, protocols, reports and
#    session records. Nothing on the site links to any of these.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
tools/
docs/
reports/
engineering-reports/
production-system/
corrections/
.github/
.claude/
Claude skill/
# Root-level governance and session documents (README, AI_SESSION_*,
# ENGINEERING_PRINCIPLES_*, REPOSITORY_STATUS). Anchored: only the root.
/*.md

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT excluded, on purpose: middleware.js, api/, vercel.json, package.json,
# SQ/, solvedQP/, meoclass1/ product pages and their content indexes,
# assets/, articles/, archive/, RulesApp/, GHGDecarb/, robots.txt, CNAME and
# the root HTML issues. /meoclass1/pastpapers/*.html (the review tree) is
# deliberately still shipped -- its retirement is a separate, pending decision.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
